    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "Cheap Only in Price, Not in Quality\n\n**Plum Smokin’ Vanilla**  \nSaw rave reviews on the sub, found it listed on Myntra during a sale for peanuts, bought it.  \nRemarkable perfume. Falls somewhere between the spicy vanilla of Babycat and the gourmand richness of TFTV. Surprising quality for the price.\n\n**Cauvery Mysore Sandal Attar Perfume**  \nVisited their store, spotted this near the counter, had some spare change, so picked it up.  \nAmazingly creamy and floral Mysore sandalwood. Yes, it uses synthetic aroma molecules, but they absolutely nailed the scent.\n\n**Theater Tragedy**  \nAnother one discovered through the sub. Used to lurk here and saw people recommending it, so bought it for my cousin. Fresh florals up front, drying down to woody vanilla and soft musk. Universally pleasant. Great presentation too.\n\n**Axe Signature Gold Dark Vanilla and Oud Wood**  \nThis was a filler buy during the Big Billion Days sale to hit the card discount threshold. Saw it, added it. Turns out it's a well-blended, simple gourmand vanilla with soft woods. No unnecessary flash. Sadly discontinued now.\n\n**Wildstone Whisky**  \nTotal surprise. Did not expect this level of creativity from a mass-market brand focused on numbers. Unique whisky-inspired perfume that leans artistic. Definitely not for everyone. I still can’t believe this one made it past approval.\n\n**BellaVita Honey Oud**  \nYes, it’s BellaVita. Infamous as always. Good for the price.  \nSits in between Montale Honey Aoud and Floris Honey Oud, though it doesn’t copy either directly. Loved it.",
        "source": "reddit",
