      {
        "text": "Online shopping is 90% guessing, 10% hoping you didn’t just buy trash\nI try to be intentional when I shop—buy things that are sustainable, safe, ethical, actually *worth* the money—but let’s be honest: online shopping makes that nearly impossible.\n\nEvery product is “eco,” “clean,” “non-toxic,” “handcrafted,” “minimalist,” or some other buzzword. Until it arrives in five layers of plastic, smells weird, and breaks in two weeks.\n\nI’m tired of:  \n❌ Fake reviews  \n❌ Greenwashed branding  \n❌ $40 “clean” products that are just scented nonsense  \n❌ Buying stuff that becomes clutter 2 months later\n\nThere should be a browser extension or app that gives you a *real* read on a product *while* you shop:  \n⚠️ This is overpriced garbage  \n✅ This is legit and built to last  \n🧪 This contains stuff you might want to avoid  \n🌍 Bonus points if it’s ethical and low-impact\n\nUntil that exists, I’ll just keep reading 47 reviews and hoping I don’t regret it.\n\nWhat’s the worst thing you’ve ever bought online that *seemed* great?",
